   "en": "But the unhappy queen of Carthage, sick at heart, finds no rest, no release into sleep; night brings [no|6,7] peace to her eyes or to her breast. Her anxieties redouble, and her love, rising up again, rages and surges on a great swell of anger. [So|26,27] she keeps returning to it, turning it over in her heart:",
