  {
   "id": 2,
   "ref": "534–539",
   "en": "'Well then, what am I to do? Should I go crawling back to my old suitors, only to be laughed at all over again, and beg the Africans, humbled, for marriage — men I [have|15,18] already refused so many times as husbands? Or should I follow the Trojan fleet instead, and obey their commanders' every last word? Because, of course, they're so grateful for the help I gave them before, and the memory of that old kindness [runs so deep|34,38]!",
   "en_marked": "'[Well then|1], [what|2] [am I to do|3]? [Should I|8] {go crawling back|Not in the Latin. experiar means should I try; the translator adds Dido's sense of humiliation.} to my [old|7] [suitors|5], {only|Added to bring out the bitterness of inrisa: she would go back just to be mocked.} [to be laughed at|6] {all over|Added for emphasis; rursus in rursusne simply means again.} [again|4], [and|9] [beg|10] [the Africans|9], [humbled|12], for [marriage|11] — [men|13] [I|14] [have|15,18] [already|17] [refused|18] [so many times|16] as [husbands|19]? [Or|21] [should I follow|27] the [Trojan|20] [fleet|22] [instead|21], [and|23] [obey|27] [their commanders'|25] [every last|24] [word|26]? [Because|28], {of course|Added to bring out the sarcasm of quiane: Dido is mocking the idea that the Trojans feel any gratitude.}, [they're so grateful|30] for [the help|29] I [gave them|32] [before|31], [and|33] [the memory|36] of that [old|37] [kindness|40] [runs so deep|34,38]!",
